1.5.9 Mutable Key Failure Experiment

Given:

Map<User, String> map = new HashMap<>();

User user = new User("A");

map.put(user, "value");

user.setId("B");

System.out.println(map.get(user));

Questions

249. What hash was used during insertion?


250. What hash is used during lookup?


251. Why can lookup fail?


252. Does the entry necessarily disappear?


253. Why is this behavior so confusing?


254. What property of keys should normally remain stable?


255. How would you fix the design?


256. Would making the entire User immutable solve the problem?


257. Should mutable business entities generally be used as hash keys?



The module explicitly requires this experiment and asks you to understand why mutable keys are dangerous. 


