---

🔥 1.5 Final Mastery Test

Round 1 — Object

You should be able to explain:

why Object exists

its position in the hierarchy

inherited methods

identity

runtime metadata

object references



---

Round 2 — Equality

Without notes, explain the complete contract:

Reflexive
Symmetric
Transitive
Consistent
Non-null

Then implement a correct equals().


---

Round 3 — Hashing

Given:

User a = new User("1");
User b = new User("1");

answer:

Are they identical?

Are they logically equal?

Must their hashes match?

Can unequal objects have the same hash?

What happens inside HashMap?



---

Round 4 — Collection Trap

Given:

Map<User, String> map = new HashMap<>();

User u = new User("A");
map.put(u, "hello");

u.setId("B");

map.get(u);

You must explain exactly why lookup can fail.


---

Round 5 — Equality + Inheritance

Given:

Money
   ↓
Voucher

you must analyze:

instanceof

getClass()

symmetry

transitivity

substitutability

canEqual()

composition

records/value objects



---

Round 6 — toString()

Given a production object containing:

ID
Name
Password
Token
Huge collection
Nested objects

design a safe toString().

You must explain:

security

performance

circular references

logging

lazy loading

side effects



---

Round 7 — Runtime Type

Given:

Animal animal = new Dog();

explain:

animal.getClass()
Animal.class
Dog.class
animal instanceof Animal
animal instanceof Dog

Then explain how framework proxies can complicate exact class checks.


---

Round 8 — Copying

Given:

Person
 └── Address

explain:

Original
   ↓
clone()
   ↓
Copy

and determine:

what is copied

what is shared

shallow vs deep copy

aliasing

mutation effects

why copy constructors may be better



---

Round 9 — Resource Management

Explain why this design is wrong:

finalize() {
    closeResource();
}

Then redesign it using:

AutoCloseable
      +
try-with-resources

and explain when Cleaner might be appropriate.


---

Round 10 — Production Debugging

You receive a production bug:

> "HashMap.get(key) sometimes returns null even though the key was inserted."



Your investigation should be:

Check equals()
       ↓
Check hashCode()
       ↓
Check key mutability
       ↓
Check object state
       ↓
Check hash distribution
       ↓
Inspect collection
       ↓
Reproduce
       ↓
Fix


